---
description: Rata architecture and privilege boundaries
alwaysApply: true
---

- Never place privileged operations in React components.
- Renderer -> Preload IPC -> Agent -> Policy -> Tool -> Adapter/Native bridge.
- Never bypass PolicyEngine for a state-changing action.
- Every new tool needs an ID, typed/schema-validated input, risk classification, confirmation policy, audit events and tests.
- Never expose generic `exec`, `eval`, shell or unrestricted filesystem APIs to the renderer or model.
- Provider implementations must stay behind an interface and must not leak into UI components.
- Character animations are presentation state only.
- Major architecture changes require an ADR.
